other value is programmed into the mode bits M[4:0], the result is UNPREDICTABLE"; the glossary (`:45062-45065`):
UNPREDICTABLE "must not halt or hang the processor"; ARMv7 (`ddi0406.txt:143212`) lets it be UNDEFINED.  Declining
the MODE FIELD only, with the instruction's other effects applied, is this emulator's choice, not an architectural
requirement; codex's pass-1 dissent (decline the whole operation) is recorded below.

