   Save default:   debugger cpsr= only      latch + return                    "arm_save_..."     dbg save, dbg both
   Load default:   debugger cpsr= only      latch + return                    "arm_load_..."     dbg both
   Asymmetries: (i) zero-SPSR (mode 0x00) is rowed on the DPI path only; arm_pop is rowed only with
   the 0x14 poison -- same helper, so a helper defect at 0x00 shows on zero spsr; a pop-local defect
   specific to 0x00 is not rowed (disclosed).  (ii) The msr decline has an I/F pin that
   distinguishes field-only from whole-op; the restores have no whole-op alternative (pc and the LDM
   loads are already done) so their I/F pin distinguishes "SPSR applied" from "CPSR write skipped".
   (iii) Load's backstop has exactly ONE carrier (dbg both); Save's has two.

2. CLAIM -> ROW (added comment sentences asserting an observable consequence)
   cpu_arm.c helper "case list MUST stay equal to Save/Load": kill 14/15/1e (domain), acc * (range)
              -- a list differing at an UNDRIVEN value (0x16, 0x18-0x1a, 0x1c-0x1d, 0x01-0x0f): NO ROW, disclosed in contract.
   Save default "a guest instruction no longer gets here": all guest rows show no "save" text; dbg save/both show it.
   Save default "announce once per CPU and return -- no exit(1)": dbg save, dbg both (alive + save).
   Save default "r8-r14 ... not saved": dbg save (SP after Load(SVC) is the never-saved 0, no ` sp').
   Load default "announce once per CPU and return": dbg both (alive + load).
   Load default "r8-r14 keep their current values": dbg both (` sp' = BOOT_SP survives).
   cpu_arm.h "each announce once per CPU, independently": dbg both (Save and Load in one instruction).
              -- independence between two DECLINE sites, and between a decline and a backstop: NO ROW, disclosed.
   msr_imm "declining the MODE FIELD only, with the rest of the write applied": kill 14/15/1e if=0.
   msr_imm "only the local mask changes: ic->arg[] is a cached translation": NO ROW (each row executes
              the MSR once; a re-execution row would be needed) -- disclosed.
   arm_pop "keeps the CURRENT mode ... every other bit from the SPSR": rst ldm m=13 if=0.
   arm_pop "No return here: the PC load below must still run": rst ldm (reaches TGT, else nofire).
   DPI "keeps the CURRENT mode ... all other bits from the SPSR": rst movs, zero spsr (m=13 if=0).
   DPI "Only when an SPSR was copied": dbg both (no "dpi S-to-pc" announce on a plant).
   DPI "no early return (pc is set)": rst movs / zero spsr (reach TGT).

3. GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD
   msr_imm guard reads ic->arg[0] M[4:0] and mask; body writes cpsr from new_value (= ic->arg[0]) &
     mask.  Same source word -- no disagreeing-state row owed.  The USR mask line runs first (usr mask row).
   arm_pop/DPI guard reads new_cpsr (the SPSR) M[4:0]; body writes cpsr from new_cpsr and decides
     the bank switch on it.  Same value.  DPI also reads cur_mode (captured before the switch) and
     spsr_copied (set by the switch's default:): disagreeing state = "current mode has no SPSR"
     (USR/SYS, or a planted reserved mode) -> dbg both rows it (planted 0x14).
   Latch: mode_warned, a per-CPU field; writers = the five announce sites only (grep mode_warned).
     A shared-bit collision is the only cross-site hazard -> dbg both.

4. PER ROW: the mutant it kills, and the observable that differs
   kill 14/15     M_d helper=1, M_drop_msr: Load backstop, m=14/15 + "load" text not "msr_imm"; M_wholeop: if=3
   kill 1e        M_range: m=1e (Load backstop)
   save 2s        M_drop_msr: m=14 at slot, then Save backstop; (pre-existing row)
   rst movs       M_drop_dpi: m=14, no "dpi S-to-pc"; M_d: same
   rst ldm        M_drop_pop: m=14, no "arm_pop"; M_pop_return: nofire (PC load skipped)
   zero spsr      M_drop_dpi: m=00 (+ Load backstop)
   acc movs       M_uncond_dpi: m=13 not m=1f (+ "dpi" announce absent but SP differs: sp)
   acc ldm        M_uncond_pop: m=13 not m=1f
   dbg save       M_save_exit (verbatim), M_save_exit_latched: dead
   dbg both       M_load_exit (verbatim), M_load_exit_latched: dead; M_save_exit: dead;
                  M_shared_latch / M_shared_saveload: " load" missing; M_dpi_uncond_call: " once" appears
   CHANNEL check: every row's channel is a readback slot or an announce line that differs under its
   named mutant; none is survive-only (all also require alive, but the readback is what kills the
   non-exit mutants).
END PRETABLE
