regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/panel_f2_20261007\grok.txt:1:I'll adjudicate the 12 dispositions against `GXEMUL-SEC/src/` at `ef577140` only, starting from the writers and the restore paths the sketch names.VERDICT: 1 of 12 dispositions wrong
regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/panel_f2_20261007\grok.txt:17:7. **7 | RIGHT:** Whole-operation decline is legal under UNPREDICTABLE, and it is the wrong policy for this guest. Measured on `MSR CPSR_c, #0x14` from boot `0xD3`: field-only MRS is `0x00000013`; whole-operation MRS is `0x000000D3`. Under `continue`, field-only takes IRQs (`cpu_dyntrans.c:206-209` is off only while `single_step`). The 17 stay on `step` and `classify()` keeps only `cpsr & 0x1f`, so both policies score 17/17 today. What whole-operation buys is that interrupt lock, and an MRS that is different from legal `#0x13`. What it loses on the restore paths is the PC write: DPI stores `cpu->pc` before the SPSR copy (`cpu_arm_instr_dpi.c:215`), and LDM(3) loads the word list before `CPSR = SPSR` (`ddi0100i.txt:8149-8161`). Declining the whole restore drops that transfer. Field-only keeps it and replaces only M[4:0].
