regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/panel_f2_20261007\ollama_kimi.txt:11:7 | RIGHT ruling; the dissent's benefit is currently zero *measured*: M2 reached 17/17 without pinning I/F, so nothing witness-distinguishes whole-op from field-only today (row (e) will pin it). Dominance argument, REASONED: field-only decline is a legal UNPREDICTABLE outcome under **both** readings of the scope sentence; whole-op decline is legal **only** if the *entire* CPSR update is UNPREDICTABLE — under the owner's own warrant (only M[4:0] unpredictable, flags/I/F effects defined), whole-op decline suppresses architecturally *defined* effects and would be the wrong one. Settling fact, if anyone disputes the warrant: ddi0100i's exact scope sentence for reserved-M MSR writes — not in the packet.
