  * the msr_imm decline clearing fewer than all five mode bits at ANY label (grid msr: G2
    declines label ^ 0x1f at all six labels; kill 03, encl2), or clearing MORE (`& ~0x3f', T lost:
    tbit, grid msr); the restore keep-mode mask letting any SPSR mode bit through (grid dpi/pop:
    G2; src rows);
  * a restore guard made unconditional, or unconditional for one label, or skipped / forced for one
    label x latch-state cell (src rows: all 40 cells; acc movs, acc ldm);
  * a WHOLE-OPERATION decline in msr_imm instead of field-only (the `if=' pin on kill rows; msr
    wide);
  * a decline OR accept taking ANY bit 31:5 from the old CPSR, or forcing it to 0 or to 1, with
    the latch SET (grid G1); with the latch CLEAR the restore paths are observed only with SPSR
    bits 31:8 SET (grid obs 0, src R2) -- a force-1 or OR-old of bits 31:8 on a FIRST DPI/pop
    decline, or a force-1 on a latch-clear restore accept, is NOT CLAIMED (MEASURED 47/47 on the
    final pass: N_pop_forceN_first, N_dpi_forceN_first, N_pop_orold_first, N_dpi_orold_first,
    E_pop_forceN_clracc -- artifacts/armmsrmodekill/opus_pass2r5_20261009/); on msr the
    latch-clear decline is held by msr wide ALONE and the latch-clear accept by grid pop's G4 p1
    cells ALONE.  (Repair 5's text claimed "with the latch clear or set (grid *: G1 complementary
    pairs; src R2/R3; tbit; msr wide)": FALSE for bits 31:8 at the restores; narrowed 2026-10-09,
    owner ruling, the Opus 5.5 seat's measurement and suggested text.) --
    this replaces the repair-3 sentence "the declined SPSR has N Z I F SET while the CPSR it
    replaces has them CLEAR" (FALSE for N and Z) and repair 4's "at EVERY decline, every restored
    bit differs" (FALSE for T at src R2/R3 and msr wide: it held only as a UNION);
  * any two of the five latch sites sharing a bit (latch rpt: all five in one process; also
